IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-sch9-ninth-schedule.l4: the Ninth Schedule (decisions of the Appellate Division that are not appealable).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 6487-6540).  Answers seam 15 of PLAN.md; the asking section is s 46, in scja2's range.
-- "The Schedule bars an appeal" is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Schedule itself takes the case out (para 3(1) "unless") or where a limb's own wording is not met;
-- NOTHING where the decision is not one of the Appellate Division.

§ `Ninth Schedule: decisions of the Appellate Division that are not appealable`

-- The facts about a decision that the Ninth Schedule turns on and that the core's Decision does not hold.
DECLARE `sch 9 facts about the decision` HAS
    `the permission given or refused was permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appeal relates only to costs or fees for hearing dates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party seeking to appeal proves a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appeal is against the part of the decision that the agreement relates to` IS A BOOLEAN

-- When the agreement that a decision is final was made (para 3(2)(a)).
DECLARE `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) when the agreement was made` IS ONE OF
    `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) before the decision was made`
    `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) after the decision was made`
    `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) at the same time as the decision`

-- Helper: one answer from several limbs.  Any limb that holds gives JUST TRUE; limbs that all fail give JUST FALSE; an unanswered limb leaves NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 the limbs taken together` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) limbs
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING limbs
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the Appellate Division in the following cases" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
         ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN way IS A `Way an order went`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 the order gave or refused` MEANS
    way EQUALS `granted unconditionally`
    OR way EQUALS `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
    OR way EQUALS refused

GIVEN way IS A `Way an order went`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 the order was made` MEANS
    way EQUALS `granted unconditionally`
    OR way EQUALS `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
    OR way EQUALS `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal`

-- The Schedule's scope: "Cases where decision of Appellate Division is not appealable".  Only the Appellate Division is its subject.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 the decision is one of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF decision's `made by` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule speaks of decisions of the Appellate Division only
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:6495 | (a) a case where the Appellate Division makes an incidental direction or
-- src:6496 | interim order under section 40(1);
@ref Ninth Schedule para 1(a) (src:6495-6496)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(a) the Appellate Division makes an incidental direction or interim order under section 40(1)` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `an incidental direction or interim order under section 40(1) or 58(1)`
       AND `sch 9 the order was made` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a case where the Appellate Division makes an incidental direction or interim order under section 40(1)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6505 | (b) a case where the Appellate Division makes a judgment or an order that
-- src:6506 | is made by consent of the parties;
@ref Ninth Schedule para 1(b) (src:6505-6506)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(b) the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties` MEANS
    IF decision's `made by consent of the parties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a case where the Appellate Division makes a judgment or an order that is made by consent of the parties"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6508 | (c) a case where the Appellate Division gives or refuses permission to
-- src:6509 | appeal against a decision of the General Division;
@ref Ninth Schedule para 1(c) (src:6508-6509)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 9 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(c) the Appellate Division gives or refuses permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `permission to appeal`
       AND `sch 9 the order gave or refused` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
       AND facts's `the permission given or refused was permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a case where the Appellate Division gives or refuses permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6513 | (d) a case where any written law expressly provides that the decision of the
-- src:6514 | Appellate Division is final or that there is no appeal from the decision
-- src:6515 | of the Appellate Division.
@ref Ninth Schedule para 1(d) (src:6513-6515)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(d) a written law expressly provides that the decision is final or that there is no appeal` MEANS
    IF decision's `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a case where any written law expressly provides that the decision of the Appellate Division is final or that there is no appeal from the decision"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6517 | 2. An appeal that relates only to costs or fees for hearing dates cannot be brought
-- src:6518 | against a decision of the Appellate Division.
@ref Ninth Schedule para 2 (src:6517-6518)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 9 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2 the appeal relates only to costs or fees for hearing dates` MEANS
    IF facts's `the appeal relates only to costs or fees for hearing dates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal that relates only to costs or fees for hearing dates cannot be brought"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6529 | (2) An agreement mentioned in sub‑paragraph (1) —
-- src:6531 | (a) may be made before or after the decision to which the agreement
-- src:6532 | relates is made; and
-- src:6534 | (b) may relate to part of a decision, in which case references in
-- src:6535 | sub‑paragraph (1) to a decision are to be read as references to that
-- src:6536 | part of the decision.
@ref Ninth Schedule para 3(2)(a) (src:6529-6536)
GIVEN timing IS A `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) when the agreement was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 3(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` MEANS
    CONSIDER timing
    WHEN `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) before the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) after the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says the agreement "may be made before or after the decision" and says nothing of an agreement made at the same moment
    WHEN `sch 9 para 3(2)(a) at the same time as the decision` THEN NOTHING

-- src:6529 | (2) An agreement mentioned in sub‑paragraph (1) —
-- src:6531 | (a) may be made before or after the decision to which the agreement
-- src:6532 | relates is made; and
-- src:6534 | (b) may relate to part of a decision, in which case references in
-- src:6535 | sub‑paragraph (1) to a decision are to be read as references to that
-- src:6536 | part of the decision.
@ref Ninth Schedule para 3(2)(b) (src:6529-6536)
-- When the agreement relates to part of a decision, the bar reaches that part only.  Appealing another part is outside the bar.
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 9 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT facts's `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision`
       OR facts's `the appeal is against the part of the decision that the agreement relates to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references in sub-paragraph (1) to a decision are to be read as references to that part of the decision"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6520 | 3.—(1) An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the Appellate
-- src:6521 | Division, where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each
-- src:6522 | party that the decision is final, unless the party seeking to appeal proves that —
-- src:6524 | (a) the decision is affected by fraud or illegality; or
-- src:6526 | (b) there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the
-- src:6527 | proceedings resulting in the decision.
@ref Ninth Schedule para 3(1) (src:6520-6527)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 9 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` MEANS
    IF decision's `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final`
    THEN IF facts's `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality`
            OR facts's `the party seeking to appeal proves a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the party seeking to appeal proves that (a) the decision is affected by fraud or illegality; or (b) there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice"
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `sch 9 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` facts
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6487 | NINTH SCHEDULE
-- src:6489 | Sections 46 and 83(1)
-- src:6491 | CASES WHERE DECISION OF
-- src:6492 | APPELLATE DIVISION IS NOT APPEALABLE
-- src:6493 | 1. An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the Appellate Division in
-- src:6494 | the following cases:
@ref Ninth Schedule (heading and para 1 opening words) (src:6487-6494)
-- Seam 15 of PLAN.md.  JUST TRUE: the Schedule says no appeal can be brought.  JUST FALSE: no limb of the Schedule bars it.  NOTHING: not a decision of the Appellate Division.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 9 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 the Appellate Division decision is a case specified in the Ninth Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 9 the decision is one of the Appellate Division` decision
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        `sch 9 the limbs taken together` (LIST
              `sch 9 para 1(a) the Appellate Division makes an incidental direction or interim order under section 40(1)` decision
            , `sch 9 para 1(b) the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties` decision
            , `sch 9 para 1(c) the Appellate Division gives or refuses permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division` decision facts
            , `sch 9 para 1(d) a written law expressly provides that the decision is final or that there is no appeal` decision
            , `sch 9 para 2 the appeal relates only to costs or fees for hearing dates` facts
            , `sch 9 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` decision facts)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule speaks of "a decision of the Appellate Division"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
